{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge","id":985410,"title":"[2E] Alternative to Mask & Dirge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T07:37:16-07:00","id":985410,"title":"[2E] Alternative to Mask & Dirge","content":"I generally like changes in 2E <b>Requiem</b>. What I really hate are how Mask and Dirge are defined as Anchors. They just seem to me like from <b>VtM</b>, not <b>VtR</b>.<br /> <br /> I am thinking about some alternative Anchors instead of this for my games. Now I have this ideas:<br /> <br /> <b>Man</b> - This anchor defines vampires once mortal nature or hers 'rational' mind. It can be seen also as higher self. Virtue equivalent.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b> - Monster part of Kindred's personality. Base instincts and wicked desires. Vice equivalent.<br /> <br /> More lower on Humanity, then more vampire is directed by his Beast over Man in him.<br /> <br /> Would this work with <b>Requiem</b>'s setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-08-2018, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:38:21-07:00","id":985439,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a huge amount of stuff tied to the mask/dirge system, so it seems reasonably easy to mod. I could see the human and Beast aspects earning a different amount of Willpower depending on your humanity.<br /> <br /> For example :<br /> 10-9 humanity gets you 3 willpower when you satisfy the human and 0 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 8-6 humanity gets you 2 willpower when you satisfy the human and 1 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 5-3 humanity gets you 1 willpower when you satisfy the human and 2 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 2-1 humanity gets you 0 willpower when you satisfy the human and 3 when you satisfy the beast<br /> <br /> That kind of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:58:49-07:00","id":985451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985439#post985439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's a huge amount of stuff tied to the mask/dirge system, so it seems reasonably easy to mod. I could see the human and Beast aspects earning a different amount of Willpower depending on your humanity.<br /> <br /> For example :<br /> 10-9 humanity gets you 3 willpower when you satisfy the human and 0 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 8-6 humanity gets you 2 willpower when you satisfy the human and 1 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 5-3 humanity gets you 1 willpower when you satisfy the human and 2 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 2-1 humanity gets you 0 willpower when you satisfy the human and 3 when you satisfy the beast<br /> <br /> That kind of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this, but feel this compulsion gnawing at the back of my brain from 20 years of storytelling in the storytelling system, to <i>divide things by 5</i>.<br /> <br /> 10-9 humanity gets you 5 willpower when you satisfy the human and 1 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 8-7 humanity gets you 4 willpower when you satisfy the human and 2 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 6-5 humanity gets you 3 willpower when you satisfy the human and 3 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 4-3 humanity gets you 2 willpower when you satisfy the human and 4 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 2-1 humanity gets you 1 willpower when you satisfy the human and 5 when you satisfy the beast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:21:55-07:00","id":985462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985439#post985439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's a huge amount of stuff tied to the mask/dirge system, so it seems reasonably easy to mod. I could see the human and Beast aspects earning a different amount of Willpower depending on your humanity.<br /> <br /> For example :<br /> 10-9 humanity gets you 3 willpower when you satisfy the human and 0 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 8-6 humanity gets you 2 willpower when you satisfy the human and 1 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 5-3 humanity gets you 1 willpower when you satisfy the human and 2 when you satisfy the beast<br /> 2-1 humanity gets you 0 willpower when you satisfy the human and 3 when you satisfy the beast<br /> <br /> That kind of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This implies that there are 2 very different people living inside of you. That is what it says to me anyway. Then you have to start thinking of 2 different personality arcs. what satisfies the human and what satisfies the beast? If it works for you though, go for it.<br /> <br /> to the Original Poster:<br /> <br /> If you do not like them defined as anchors, change the way that you look at it. What works for my groups is to look at the Mask as what you show to other people. You are different when you are with your boss, your friends, or in public. It's not a &quot;I am a jester so I better crack a joke to get willpower&quot; situation, but It's more of everyone knows you crack jokes because it's who you are to them. You tell jokes at inappropriate times to alleviate the heaviness. It just becomes part of you.<br /> <br /> The dirge is more like who you are when no one is looking, who you are when you are free to be yourself. Like a junkie. You try to hide it, you try not to let people know, but you cant help yourself. The dirge is when you let a little of that mask slip to show who you really are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:30:45-07:00","id":985466,"title":"","content":"Good idea, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7104\" data-vbnamecard=\"7104\">S. Brechen</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> ! Will jive with my basic ideas on those Anchors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And so, here are examples of Man and Beast Anchors...<br /> <br /> Example <b>Man</b> - Most of Archetypes in <b>Vampire: Requiem</b> 2E corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Example <b>Beasts</b>:<ul><li><i>Predator</i> - You live to hunt and playing with mortals is your game.</li> <li><i>Hungry</i> - Blood is all that matters - need to have maximum Vitea all the time. Get's Willpower when refilling Vitea in same scene.</li> <li><i>Monster</i> - Monster exists to torment, frighten, and destroy. She loathes existence, and spreads that loathing wherever she goes.</li> <li><i>Deviant</i> - Deviant lives to flout norms and break traditional expectations. She isn\u2019t concerned with rebellion; she\u2019s concerned with crime, sin, and debauchery.</li> <li><i>Puppeteer</i> - Blood is powerful bond. By chaining others to you, you regain you sense of control.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-11-2016, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:37:28-07:00","id":985472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985462#post985462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do not like them defined as anchors, change the way that you look at it. What works for my groups is to look at the Mask as what you show to other people. You are different when you are with your boss, your friends, or in public. It's not a &quot;I am a jester so I better crack a joke to get willpower&quot; situation, but It's more of everyone knows you crack jokes because it's who you are to them. You tell jokes at inappropriate times to alleviate the heaviness. It just becomes part of you.<br /> <br /> The dirge is more like who you are when no one is looking, who you are when you are free to be yourself. Like a junkie. You try to hide it, you try not to let people know, but you cant help yourself. The dirge is when you let a little of that mask slip to show who you really are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand as this how it should work. The problem is that it not working for me - it didn't in <b>VtM</b> plays ( with similar Anchors ideas ), it did not when I run <b>VtR</b> 2E two sessions. Having 'hidden archetype' just is wasting of archetype slot, in my POV. Don't worry, I have the same problem with <i>Mask &amp; Mien</i> in <b>Changeling</b> 2E playtest - I just do not like those <i>'I have secret persona underneath that is not role played 90% of time' </i>Archetypes concepts.<br /> <br /> I much more liked straight forward <i>Virtue &amp; Vice</i> systems ( one of reasons why I liked 1E <b>Requiem</b> over <b>Masquerade</b> ) and would use them in <b>VtR</b> 2E - if I did not see this Man-Beast duality as more important to running <b>Vampire</b> game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:25:13-07:00","id":985540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985472#post985472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand as this how it should work. The problem is that it not working for me - it didn't in <b>VtM</b> plays ( with similar Anchors ideas ), it did not when I run <b>VtR</b> 2E two sessions. Having 'hidden archetype' just is wasting of archetype slot, in my POV. Don't worry, I have the same problem with <i>Mask &amp; Mien</i> in <b>Changeling</b> 2E playtest - I just do not like those <i>'I have secret persona underneath that is not role played 90% of time' </i>Archetypes concepts.<br /> <br /> I much more liked straight forward <i>Virtue &amp; Vice</i> systems ( one of reasons why I liked 1E <b>Requiem</b> over <b>Masquerade</b> ) and would use them in <b>VtR</b> 2E - if I did not see this Man-Beast duality as more important to running <b>Vampire</b> game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont look at it as a secret persona, something that has to be kept secret or that isnt roleplayed. I think of it more as a fundamental character trait. A personality trait that is ALWAYS there. for example... I am addicted to my phone. Totally texting and checking emails and facebook all the time or whatever. Even though I know I shouldnt be. (case in point.. right now) My dirge would be junkie. It's just part of who I am, my best friends know it. the people who spend time with me know it, but the dude down the street doesnt know that. It's not something I would need to point out in game like &quot;I am going to check my phone because I need to hit my dirge and get will power&quot; but in the little things. The prince is giving a super important speech, I pull out my phone and facebook about it. or we are driving to the important mission thing and a text comes in so I have to pull over and check it. I waste time getting to the objective because I stopped to tell my mom I was cruising with friends. Think of the mask and dirge as a vice and a virtue, just a little bit more specific of vices and virtues. Your virtue is jester, everyone comes to appreciate your humor. Your vice is authoritarian, you just have to be on top no matter what. Even a vice, like Monster. You dont have to keep kicking the guy when he is down, but you like to, you want to. It's just part of who you are. <br /> <br /> I dont see them as any less of who you are as your eye color. It is just something that is part of you. I am just trying to help understand where you're coming from to give advice for alternatives. I am not sure thinking of yourself as two different people is going to solve your problem. That might actually be worse because then you have to play the vampire, then you have to play the beast. suddenly you are trying to play two different creatures... I think vampires are far more entwined than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:41:13-07:00","id":985552,"title":"","content":"Err... If you don't like Mask and Dirge, by all means, house rule them. But Dirge is not meant to be a &quot;hidden persona that isn't role played 90% of the time&quot; any more than Vice is. <br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer to look at Mask and Dirge less as &quot;who you are with humans/other people&quot; and &quot;who you are when you're alone&quot;, and more as &quot;how you express your Masquerade&quot; and &quot;how you express your Requiem.&quot; Those were, after all, the anchors names for most of development, and got changed shortly before the final release to avoid ambiguity with other concepts in the game that use the same terms (as I expect will likely happen with Maque and Mein in Changeling as well). The Mask is the facade of humanity you wear, among humans, among vampires, and even when you're alone. It's who you tell yourself and others you are so you can keep up the illusion that you're not a walking corpse possessed by an inhuman Beast. The Dirge, the Requiem, is what you do with your immortality. Like Vice, it's an indulgence that you may be ashamed of, but nonetheless fulfills you. It's your answer to &quot;what do I do now that I'm a vampire?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:54:03-07:00","id":985563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985552#post985552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mask is the facade of humanity you wear, among humans, among vampires, and even when you're alone. It's who you tell yourself and others you are so you can keep up the illusion that you're not a walking corpse possessed by an inhuman Beast. The Dirge, the Requiem, is what you do with your immortality. Like Vice, it's an indulgence that you may be ashamed of, but nonetheless fulfills you. It's your answer to &quot;what do I do now that I'm a vampire?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And 90% of game time it's 'I'm my Mask' because you show it on the outside - with mortals, with vampires, even your coterie guys. Dirge come as 'And my masterplan is... ' moments by your own definition - and this asymmetry is very disturbing in play. Not to mention it put's aside Man-Beast dichotomy of setting.<br /> <br /> As to Virute &amp; Vice balance - maybe in <b>Vampire</b> it does not work that way, but in <b>Mage </b>games run by me V&amp;V are more or less equal in screen time from players. Well, maybe Vice a bit higher chance to show up - it is World of (Chronicles of) Darkness in the end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-11-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:03:48-07:00","id":985579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985563#post985563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And 90% of game time it's 'I'm my Mask' because you show it on the outside - with mortals, with vampires, even your coterie guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, 100% of the time it should be both. Your Dirge isn't a secret, it's just what you do with your Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985563#post985563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dirge come as 'And my masterplan is... ' moments by your own definition - and this asymmetry is very disturbing in play. Not to mention it put's aside Man-Beast dichotomy of setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not your master plan or your secret ambition. It's just where you fit into vampire society. Have you read Danse Macabre? Look at the Masquerade and Requiem Merits from that book. They're like vampire-specific versions of Professional Training, and they're the concepts that eventually became Mask and Dirge in second edition. It's not &quot;who you pretend to be&quot; and &quot;who you really are&quot;, it's &quot;what you do to maintain the appearance of humanity&quot; and &quot;what you do to enjoy being a vampire&quot;. Neither of those things need to be kept hidden, and neither of them are more or less your true self. They're both just expressions of how you live your unlife.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985563#post985563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to Virute &amp; Vice balance - maybe in <b>Vampire</b> it does not work that way, but in <b>Mage </b>games run by me V&amp;V are more or less equal in screen time from players. Well, maybe Vice a bit higher chance to show up - it is World of (Chronicles of) Darkness in the end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As should Mask and Dirge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:18:41-07:00","id":985594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985563#post985563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And 90% of game time it's 'I'm my Mask' because you show it on the outside - with mortals, with vampires, even your coterie guys. Dirge come as 'And my masterplan is... ' moments by your own definition - and this asymmetry is very disturbing in play. Not to mention it put's aside Man-Beast dichotomy of setting.<br /> <br /> As to Virute &amp; Vice balance - maybe in <b>Vampire</b> it does not work that way, but in <b>Mage </b>games run by me V&amp;V are more or less equal in screen time from players. Well, maybe Vice a bit higher chance to show up - it is World of (Chronicles of) Darkness in the end. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am right there with Charlaquinn. We are very similar on what works for us and I assume, our groups. I have not had trouble getting my vices /dirges out there for &quot;screen time&quot;. I am not saying this is your case, I am just saying that sometimes it happens, and that sometimes on the forums is a lot.. People come looking for help on changing things, but they do not fully understand on how to use the things as written. I think how much time your masks and dirges, or masquerades and requiems or ever you want to call it, gets as much screen time as the player wants it to have. <br /> <br /> I had a vampire who had Monster.. and he was always trying to tick people off and goad them into fighting so he could kick the crap out of them and call it self defense. <br /> I have a player currently who has Child and is constantly doing childish things just to get reactions out of people. He dominates people and tells them they love some other person just so he can see them hit on the other person and giggle about it in the corner. Or tells people to sleep on the job, then calls the boss to get them in trouble. Ect.. <br /> Another player has junkie ( sex ) and is always off looking for the next score... even when we should be doing something important, like saving the world. <br /> <br /> Though in the same game, I have a player with Deviant as a dirge and is constantly saying &quot; I need to get willpower back, If I do this does deviant count?&quot; most often it doesn't because he doesn't quite grasp what it's meant to be. Or it is just ridiculous stuff that frustrates the other players because it makes no sense. It is so far out of character, but he is just trying to get that willpower back it doesn't matter to him. <br /> <br /> If anyone has played dnd 3.5 there was a list of character traits you could roll for randomly. I thought it was great for building a character, especially for those who didn't know how to add depth to their paper. While not exactly the same. I do feel that mask/dirge is very very close to that. They are ultimately just tools to help flesh out your character and if calling them a mask and a dirge doesn't work for you, call them something else. If the list doesnt work for you add new things to the list. <br /> <br /> But I don't recommend having something that your player wants and something your beast wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:29:55-07:00","id":985605,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and don't get me wrong - I'm not trying to tell you not to change Mask and Dirge if they're not working for your group. By all means, do. I just want to point out that the reasons you give for having trouble with Mask and Dirge aren't consistent with my understanding of what Mask and Dirge represent, so maybe your issues can be resolved without needing to house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:42:45-07:00","id":985608,"title":"","content":"I read what is in 2E corebook, not 1E line, as we using 2E rules. In corebook, Mask &amp; Dirge are literally defined as this:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Mask</b><br /> Mask is the bearing Kindred present to the world. It\u2019s the fa\u00e7ade, the pretty lie. It\u2019s the excuse for why he can\u2019t stay for breakfast in the morning. It\u2019s the reason she gives the cab driver for dropping her off near an abandoned warehouse at odd hours of the night. It\u2019s his excuse for barely touching his dinner.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Dirge</b><br /> The Dirge is the truth behind the lies. It\u2019s the vampire\u2019s secret self; it\u2019s who he is when the lights are off and nobody is present to witness his dirtiest moments. It\u2019s his dark indulgence. It\u2019s the self-loathing she will never admit. It\u2019s his desire for an end. It\u2019s her need for companionship. </i><br /> <br /> It reads 'fa\u00e7ade' and 'secret self', literally. I do not know what is in 1E gameline alternative, but by 2E rules, they sound as '90% gameplay' and 'Masterplan/Drama scenes'.<br /> <br /> It's still off topic - <b>Subject for this discussion is hammering some good alternatives to original Anchors.</b> From my reading of some 1E books and 2E <b>Requiem</b> corebook, Beast is a bit absent as character trait. Corebook says about 'alien person' on it, but beside lowering Humanity Trait, there is not concrete idea on that. With Beast as Anchor, we can easily explore it in narrative of 2E games, just like Torment is Anchor in 2E <b>Promethean</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:49:26-07:00","id":985611,"title":"","content":"Ok, if you insist on a literal interpretation that doesn't work for you and requires you to house rule instead of a more nuanced interpretation that might resolve your issues without having to change anything, that's your perogative. I'll leave you to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:01:49-07:00","id":985616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985608#post985608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read what is in 2E corebook, not 1E line, as we using 2E rules. In corebook, Mask &amp; Dirge are literally defined as this:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Mask</b><br /> Mask is the bearing Kindred present to the world. It\u2019s the fa\u00e7ade, the pretty lie. It\u2019s the excuse for why he can\u2019t stay for breakfast in the morning. It\u2019s the reason she gives the cab driver for dropping her off near an abandoned warehouse at odd hours of the night. It\u2019s his excuse for barely touching his dinner.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Dirge</b><br /> The Dirge is the truth behind the lies. It\u2019s the vampire\u2019s secret self; it\u2019s who he is when the lights are off and nobody is present to witness his dirtiest moments. It\u2019s his dark indulgence. It\u2019s the self-loathing she will never admit. It\u2019s his desire for an end. It\u2019s her need for companionship. </i><br /> <br /> It reads 'fa\u00e7ade' and 'secret self', literally. I do not know what is in 1E gameline alternative, but by 2E rules, they sound as '90% gameplay' and 'Masterplan/Drama scenes'.<br /> <br /> It's still off topic - <b>Subject for this discussion is hammering some good alternatives to original Anchors.</b> From my reading of some 1E books and 2E <b>Requiem</b> corebook, Beast is a bit absent as character trait. Corebook says about 'alien person' on it, but beside lowering Humanity Trait, there is not concrete idea on that. With Beast as Anchor, we can easily explore it in narrative of 2E games, just like Torment is Anchor in 2E <b>Promethean</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out what it says on pp 80-81, though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Choose a Mask and a Dirge for your character. Whereas a mortal character has a Virtue and a Vice, Kindred characters have Masks and Dirges.<br /> <br /> Kindred wear Masks in public. A Mask is the persona she shows the prey. The Mask is the pretty lie, the identity that keeps her walking among the flock as an insider, even though she\u2019s nothing of the sort. It reflects how she deals with human society.<br /> <br /> <b>The Dirge is who she is</b> behind closed doors, and <b>when dealing with other Kindred.</b> A Dirge is the harsh truth to which she clings. It\u2019s the grounding point to which she always returns. <b>When she walks the halls of Elysium, and works within her covenant, she presents her Dirge.</b> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:34:11-07:00","id":985636,"title":"","content":"I like the Mask and Dirge system because they're a track for what your character is becoming, for the two aspects of the character that are pulling them in opposite directions. Early in your Requiem, they're likely to be more or less complementary. One is a reflection of the other; but as you get older, as you grow disillusioned and fall out of step with your touchstones, that mask slowly becomes just another tool you use to achieve your dirge, or a vestigial remnant from your mortal life.<br /> <br /> Let's say you're a bon vivant socialite embraced as a Daeva. You love people. You find their experiences fascinating, you find the things they have to teach you and share with you fascinating. You pride yourselves on being able to easily fit in with everyone from BoHo artists and musicians to high-heeled socialites to lifestyle surfers. You love all of them, but most of all, you love the breadth of things they've made you feel. You don't need to be the center of attention. You'd rather just soak in the pure rush of being somewhere new, with someone extraordinary, doing something outside of any reasonable comfort zone. You have the money and the means to do whatever you want, and goddammit, you aren't going to squander it. Your mask might be social chameleon, and your dirge might be experience junkie. Neither of these is a sham. They're both reflections of the same core self, and each reflects off the other. They aren't at odds with each other, and fulfilling your mask has a decent chance of also fulfilling your dirge.<br /> <br /> Now fast forward some years. You've flitted from group to group. You've tasted practically everything the city has to offer, and those friends you once loved, they're gone. Some of them died: from accidents or overdoses or more mundane tragedy. But the unlucky ones have retired to the hills, living conventional lives with conventional jobs and conventional families. So you try to integrate yourself into new groups. You figure you'll be a muse. The tragedy is, the one thing you thought would never bore you does. There's no mystery to <i>people</i> anymore. Most of the time you can guess what someone will say or do before they can even think it, and even moving to the fringes of society hasn't helped much. Sure, you can tag along with violent anarchists and fringe artists as much as you like, but they don't really have anything to show you anymore, and your social skills? They've become parasitic. Because new experience requires a push. What will happen when you push that beautiful sculptor to press the limits of his craft and his sanity? Can you drive that couple to jealous murder through subtle whispers and implied infidelities? And what does the epitome of human desperation look like?<br /> <br /> Both the mask and the dirge started as a symbiotic relationship, two entwined character values. Neither was hidden. Both were healthy or at least organic. I like it because it's not just about recovering willpower, it's about mapping how far your character drifts from who they were to what they've become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-11-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T22:42:01-07:00","id":985955,"title":"","content":"Which all is off-topic as I pointed that talking on Mask&amp;Dirge is <i>not</i> the place for it. I made topic on alternative for them, not talking how default Anchors works. If you want to talk about Mask&amp;Dirge, made other topic for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Could we return to subject of <i>this</i> topic and talk about alternatives to them?</b> Like proposed by me <i>Man &amp; Beast</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2016, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:42:53-07:00","id":986100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985955#post985955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which all is off-topic as I pointed that talking on Mask&amp;Dirge is <i>not</i> the place for it. I made topic on alternative for them, not talking how default Anchors works. If you want to talk about Mask&amp;Dirge, made other topic for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Could we return to subject of <i>this</i> topic and talk about alternatives to them?</b> Like proposed by me <i>Man &amp; Beast</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The whole reason everyone is explaining how they work and why the way they work the way they do...is because if we don't understand what it is you do not like about them or don't understand about them, we can't give you good advice on an alternative. We tried to give you alternative uses and ideas for making them work, but you are now saying that is &quot;off-topic&quot; so I am not sure how we can help you further. <br /> <br /> If you like your man/beast alternative, go for it. Do what works for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:06:14-07:00","id":986290,"title":"","content":"I interpret Mask and Dirge like Schwarzenegger film True Lies: face with common people, face with badass people. If this not works for you for whatever reason, (and I interpret that is because for you it doesn't reflect enougth the dark side of the beast and the struggle inside the vampire, correct me if I am wrong), change it.<br /> <br /> I think, and is a personal opinion, that Mask and Dirge where not made to reflect this struggle, they were made to reflect the two worlds where the vampire have to dwell (True Lies example again: your wife, daughter, friends VS spies, goberment agents, terrorists).<br /> <br /> Now, as for alternate rules that can help you to reflect with words and force to interpret the inner conflict, I think of two sources:<br /> <br /> - Kindred of The East: vampires hace a P'o nature (that is, their darker self) that is always trying to make them fall.<br /> - Werewolf the Forsaken 2E: does a good job with Blood / Bone natures, the aspects that reflects the man and wolf. You can use it to reflect the Man / Beast dicotomy I think you seek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 10-12-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T23:54:58-08:00","id":1004275,"title":"","content":"I asked <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24\" data-vbnamecard=\"24\">Mr Gone</a> to make tweaked sheet for <b>Requiem</b> 2E with Man &amp; Beast archetypes. If any one is interested in this simple hack - here is char sheet to be used. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_4-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_4-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_4-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_4-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now I can finally sheet for my London Prince from Ordo Dracul secret faction - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004274-2e-tremere-as-ordo-dracul-and-mekhet-bloodline\">Tremere</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T02:53:20-08:00","id":1004313,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this &quot;Man and Beast&quot; idea is literally just Mask and Dirge, except now you're actually <i>doing it right</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T03:46:18-08:00","id":1004322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004313#post1004313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this &quot;Man and Beast&quot; idea is literally just Mask and Dirge, except now you're actually <i>doing it right</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not seen this from reading your comments and 2E corebook definitions - Mask and Dirge sound to me more about 'showing to morals' and 'showing to vampires', working beside the same ( even using <i>exactly</i> same archetypes ). Man and Beast are a lot more like Blood and Bone from <b>Werewolf </b>or Elpis and Torment from <b>Promethean </b>- both are in you, all the time. Man is more 'sane' part of character, Beast is more 'predatory' one.<br /> <br /> But whatever - if new labels work more with the previous intent of developers, more kudos to myself for cracking it on my own. Or I just play the game more like neogothic tale of monster inside of vampire than weird 'what I show to humans / what I show to Kindred'.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, I will probably change in 2E<b> Changeling</b> it's own Anchors ideas if they do not sound as working with mine take on final release. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ( I have totally different takes on Characters Anchors compared to <b>David Hill</b>, on general, as it seems. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-17-2016, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T04:05:49-08:00","id":1004327,"title":"","content":"Mask and dirge are the side you <i>prefer</i> to show to mortals and vampires, respectively. They're both very much a part of you, and you are sometimes going to slip and show the other, such as when you feed or maybe when you're in a casual setting with your coterie.<br /> <br /> The Mask is a lie, but it's ultimately one you tell <i>yourself</i> before you tell anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":"11-17-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:29:05-08:00","id":1004375,"title":"","content":"Mask is the demeanor you choose to show the world. Dirge is the side of you that you hide (especially from other vampires) because it's a base for your sense of identity, and your dark desires that could otherwise be exploited by others.<br /> <br /> From page 84:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">&quot;The Dirge is the truth behind the lies. It\u2019s the vampire\u2019s secret self; it\u2019s who he is when the lights are off and nobody is present to witness his dirtiest moments. It\u2019s his dark indulgence. It\u2019s the self-loathing she will never admit. It\u2019s his desire for an end. It\u2019s her need for companionship.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:04:05-08:00","id":1004388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004375#post1004375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mask is the demeanor you choose to show the world. Dirge is the side of you that you hide (<b>especially from other vampires</b>) because it's a base for your sense of identity, and your dark desires that could otherwise be exploited by others.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'mma go ahead an re-quote the bit Resplendent Fire did last page: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Dirge is who she is</b><i> behind closed doors, and </i><b>when dealing with other Kindred.</b><i> A Dirge is the harsh truth to which she clings. It\u2019s the grounding point to which she always returns. </i><b>When she walks the halls of Elysium, and works within her covenant, she presents her Dirge.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T08:13:41-08:00","id":1004432,"title":"","content":"Mask and Dirge are both presented to vampires at times. Sometimes simultaneously. To follow the &quot;Unlife is a dance&quot; metaphor from which the Anchors derive their names, your Mask is the costume you wear to the ball and your Dirge is the song you dance to. You can, in fact, wear a mask and dance to a dirge at the same time. &quot;Who you pretend to be&quot; and &quot;what you do with your unlife&quot; aren't mutually exclusive things, and don't even have to be at odds with each other at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-17-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:12:35-08:00","id":1004504,"title":"","content":"Once again, I point this topic is for talking about <i>alternatives</i> to Mask &amp; Dirge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you want to talk the nuances of official ones, make other topic for it - you are beating a dead horse here, in my POV. If you have <b>other</b> ideas than Man &amp; Beast Anchors - I'm also curious of those takes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:16:49-08:00","id":1004536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004504#post1004504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, I point this topic is for talking about <i>alternatives</i> to Mask &amp; Dirge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you want to talk the nuances of official ones, make other topic for it - you are beating a dead horse here, in my POV. If you have <b>other</b> ideas than Man &amp; Beast Anchors - I'm also curious of those takes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And, once again, the reason you're getting so much discussion of Mask and Dirge is that you made a thread saying you don't like Mask and Dirge based on an inaccurate assessment of them, and then the traits you replaced them with are effectively what Mask and Dirge actually are. People are trying to explain to you that you're effectively just changing the names and then running them as intended, and then some of us are also quibbling over the specific details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T12:54:43-08:00","id":1004587,"title":"","content":"I would not say that Man &amp; Beast are the same as Mask &amp; Dirge. The original are about how humans/vampires are observing you - they can be similar to Man, maybe, but Beast is just primal 'wickedness' of character - it does have <b>nothing </b>to how it is seen by others. They only share some archetypes just because part of them works in both paradigm.<br /> <br /> You cannot point to me that Beast works as Mask or Dirge alone, when Beast is Vice equivalent, like Blood in <b>Werewolf</b> or Torment in <b>Promethean</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:25:35-08:00","id":1004599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004587#post1004587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not say that Man &amp; Beast are the same as Mask &amp; Dirge. The original are about how humans/vampires are observing you - they can be similar to Man, maybe, but Beast is just primal 'wickedness' of character - it does have <b>nothing </b>to how it is seen by others. They only share some archetypes just because part of them works in both paradigm.<br /> <br /> You cannot point to me that Beast works as Mask or Dirge alone, when Beast is Vice equivalent, like Blood in <b>Werewolf</b> or Torment in <b>Promethean</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Beast Archetype is absolutely Dirge. Dirge isn't about how you're observed either, Dirge is what you do with your Requiem; it's you without the pretense of humanity. In other words, it's what the Beast, the embodiment of your vampiric self, wants. You present it as base urges, while the book presents it as secret desires, but ultimately there's no difference, except that the latter emphasizes the pretense inherent in The Requiem. The show of turning your darkest, most monstrous desires into a dance. A performance.<br /> <br /> Likewise, your Man Archetype is the side of you that is still grounded in the world of the living, which is exactly what Mask is. Again, whether it's &quot;the human you struggle to be in spite of the Beast&quot; or &quot;the human you are so good at pretending to be that you've fooled even yourself&quot;, there's no practical difference. The latter just emphasizes the fact that the struggle is a lie. A game of make-believe that vampires willingly participate in so they can keep telling themselves that the Man, not the Beast, is who they really are.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, whether you call it Man and Beast or Mask and Dirge, either way it's just your human side and your monster side. The choice to present it in terms of the dance metaphor just keeps it more consistent with Requiem's themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are you going to do to make it through tonight? What about tomorrow night? And after the deeds are done and your belly\u2019s full, how are you going to live with yourself? What are you going to do with your damnation that makes it worth all the sins along the way?<br /> That\u2019s the <s>Requiem</s> Dirge<br /> <br /> That\u2019s only half the question, though. Mortals are dinner, but they\u2019re also what you\u2019ve got for dates. No matter how<br /> callous you become, you\u2019ll need to move among them. How will you keep your connection to Humanity, even as a sham?<br /> That\u2019s the <s>Masquerade</s> Mask. </div> </div> </div>Modified slightly for emphasis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-17-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T21:13:05-08:00","id":1004798,"title":"","content":"I do not agree with Dirge/Requiem part, as definition sounds much more noble than using of Beast in my mind. It's not performance, not dance, it's dark urges, Beasts whisperers in vampires ear, that he listen to, from time to time. Beast must be Dark Passenger of character, like from<b> Dexter</b> show.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2QB8kDZPIGw\" data-code=\"2QB8kDZPIGw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2QB8kDZPIGw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Just see on those examples of Beast:<ul><li><i>Predator</i> - You live to hunt and playing with mortals is your game.</li> <li><i>Hungry</i> - Blood is all that matters - need to have maximum Vitea all the time. Get's Willpower when refilling Vitea in same scene.</li> <li><i>Monster</i> - Monster exists to torment, frighten, and destroy. She loathes existence, and spreads that loathing wherever she goes.</li> <li><i>Deviant</i> - Deviant lives to flout norms and break traditional expectations. She isn\u2019t concerned with rebellion; she\u2019s concerned with crime, sin, and debauchery.</li> <li><i>Puppeteer</i> - Blood is powerful bond. By chaining others to you, you regain you sense of control.</li> </ul>Dirge sounds like things that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_de_Pointe_du_Lac\" target=\"_blank\">Louis de Pointe du Lac</a> would have 'Melancholic' or even 'Emo' defined. In Beast variant it would be 'Death Risking' or even 'Predator' - as his most defined dark aspect that he secretly was enjoining being hunter with mortals ( just see him after transformation of Claudia in movie, even than for one century he was resisting it ).<br /> <br /> But whatever - maybe I just reinvented wheel with much more straight forward and evocative names for Anchors. If that is, game just solved one of greatest problems I had with 2E <b>Requiem</b> changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T21:45:47-08:00","id":1004807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004798#post1004798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree with Dirge/Requiem part, as definition sounds much more noble than using of Beast in my mind. It's not performance, not dance, it's dark urges, Beasts whisperers in vampires ear, that he listen to, from time to time. Beast must be Dark Passenger of character, like from<b> Dexter</b> show.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing my point. Dirge <i>is</i> dark urges, the reason it's presented as something elegant is because vampires are pretentious and deluded, and presenting their dark urges as a dance is exactly the sort of thing they do all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004798#post1004798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just see on those examples of Beast:<ul><li><i>Predator</i> - You live to hunt and playing with mortals is your game.</li> <li><i>Hungry</i> - Blood is all that matters - need to have maximum Vitea all the time. Get's Willpower when refilling Vitea in same scene.</li> <li><i>Monster</i> - Monster exists to torment, frighten, and destroy. She loathes existence, and spreads that loathing wherever she goes.</li> <li><i>Deviant</i> - Deviant lives to flout norms and break traditional expectations. She isn\u2019t concerned with rebellion; she\u2019s concerned with crime, sin, and debauchery.</li> <li><i>Puppeteer</i> - Blood is powerful bond. By chaining others to you, you regain you sense of control.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Those all sound like Archetypes, which could easily be Masks or Dirges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004798#post1004798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dirge sounds like things that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_de_Pointe_du_Lac\" target=\"_blank\">Louis de Pointe du Lac</a> would have 'Melancholic' or even 'Emo' defined. In Beast variant it would be 'Death Risking' or even 'Predator' - as his most defined dark aspect that he secretly was enjoining being hunter with mortals ( just see him after transformation of Claudia in movie, even than for one century he was resisting it ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Melancholic is Louis' <i>Mask</i>. It's the persona he puts on to convince Lestat, Claudia, Armand, the interviewer, and most importantly himself, that he still has a semblance of humanity. Risking death would probably be the &quot;All Willpower&quot; mode of his Mask. His Dirge <i>would</i> probably be something like Predator, because as you observed, that is the dark desire he hides behind his mask.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004798#post1004798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But whatever - maybe I just reinvented wheel with much more straight forward and evocative names for Anchors. If that is, game just solved one of greatest problems I had with 2E <b>Requiem</b> changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>More straightforward? maybe. More evocative? on the contrary, you've taken poetic names that tie into an ongoing metaphor that is so central to the game it's literally one of the listed themes and swapped them for names that are almost painfully on-the-nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T00:20:11-08:00","id":1004825,"title":"","content":"Topic is still valid for those that have other ideas for alternative Anchors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1004807#post1004807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More straightforward? maybe. More evocative? on the contrary, you've taken poetic names that tie into an ongoing metaphor that is so central to the game it's literally one of the listed themes and swapped them for names that are almost painfully on-the-nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's more simpler, but I like them as this way. Poetic is sometimes just <i>too</i> flowery, missing point for some men. If I still do use Archetypes as needed, my renaming only fulfilled points of 2E change in first place, not pushing me of the basic assumptions of the game. More kudos to me then, from translating what designers had in mind for use of common gamers, not understanding metaphor in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-18-2016, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:41:14-08:00","id":1005386,"title":"","content":"I could see a ordo dracul perhaps describe it a little different. Instead of man and beast. <br /> <br /> Perhaps Id and Ego. <br /> <br /> Your ID is the sum total of your wants. <br /> The Ego is who you try to be. <br /> <br /> Very similar to man vs beast, but not every action has to be related to primal instinct. <br /> <br /> A little Freudian but then again he was big into interpreting things in a very sexual nature and vampire can be that way as well. So maybe fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","user":"overload","date":". 11-19-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T09:24:56-07:00","id":1063254,"title":"","content":"Why not say something more on the nose, if that's the direction you want? Human/Monster, Civil/Creature, Life/Unlife, Suit/Fang, Flesh/Blood.<br /> Interpretation of the original is valid, and personal connotations aside any of the above are equally valid. There is no <i>right </i>way to go through the rules, only your way. If you want to change something, change it, alter it, replace it, ignore it.<br /> <br /> The rules as written are<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Not gospel</li> <li>Open to interpretation</li> <li>Only extant in your world to the point that you allow them to be</li> <li>An incomplete toolset for you to construct a world with</li> </ol>Further, it doesn't matter which rules you leave out, as long as you look to the consequences of omission. It doesn't matter which rules you change, as long as you're aware of what that means to the world at large. And it doesn't matter if someone disagrees, provided they aren't at your gaming table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T09:45:48-07:00","id":1063273,"title":"","content":"I don't honestly see the difference between calling it Mask and Dirge and Man and Beast. They're exactly the same thing, it's just that the first is written in flowery, pretentious Kindred language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T18:32:08-07:00","id":1063695,"title":"","content":"If we're renaming them, perhaps it would be thematic to come up with suitable names for characters of different Clans and Covenants? <br /> Daeva: Masquerade vs Requiem (Flowery, metaphorical)<br /> Gangrel: Man vs Beast (immediate and short)<br /> Mekhet: ? vs Shadow (Mystical, not obvious meanings)<br /> Nosferatu: Human vs Monster (like Gangrel, but focus on how inhuman the Nosferatu perceive themselves as)<br /> Ventrue: Mask vs Dirge (TBH, I still prefer Masquerade vs Requiem for them as well as the Daeva, but I always have issues differentiating Daeva and Ventrue themes for some reason.)<br /> <br /> Carthians: Man vs Tyrant? (They see humanity as worth imitating? not so happy with this one)<br /> Circle: Mortal vs Goddess (They disdain humanity, and so emphasize acting with their deeper darker passions)<br /> Sanctum: Humanity vs the Devil (Similar to the Circle, but for different reasons. The Mask is what allows them to perform their intentions a mongst their &quot;flock&quot; and charges)<br /> Invictus: Masquerade vs Requiem (Masquerade keepers, eloquent)<br /> Ordo: Ego vs Id (I really like this one, pseudo-scientific)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T18:37:17-07:00","id":1063698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1063695#post1063695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're renaming them, perhaps it would be thematic to come up with suitable names for characters of different Clans and Covenants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not opposed to the Clan-specific idea, but I question having both Clan and Covenant. Does one supercede the other, in your view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T19:31:55-07:00","id":1063719,"title":"","content":"Whichever one your character more strongly identifies with, I'd say. I personally wouldn't use it, just a fun little thought exercise I think. Or perhaps whichever one the chronicle as a whole emphasizes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T22:54:10-07:00","id":1063749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1063695#post1063695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circle: Mortal vs Goddess (They disdain humanity, and so emphasize acting with their deeper darker passions)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with Maiden vs. Crone. The Circle doesn't disdain humanity, they view both the woman and the beast as equal aspects of the vampire and don't resent either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T03:40:29-07:00","id":1063791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=1063749#post1063749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would go with Maiden vs. Crone. The Circle doesn't disdain humanity, they view both the woman and the beast as equal aspects of the vampire and don't resent either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that's even better, I was struggling with that one. I personally find the Clan versions more... fitting, generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T05:06:23-08:00","id":1173196,"title":"","content":"For information and usability - Mr. Gone done char sheets with Man &amp; Beast as Anchors<ul><li>VtR 2E 4-Page Sheet with Man &amp; Beast</li> </ul><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_4-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a><ul><li>VtR 2E NPCs Sheet with Man &amp; Beast</li> </ul><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_2ndED_NPCSheet2-Pagev2_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T10:06:19-08:00","id":1173252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/985410-2e-alternative-to-mask-dirge?p=985466#post985466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example <b>Beasts</b>:<ul><li><i>Predator</i> - You live to hunt and playing with mortals is your game.</li> <li><i>Hungry</i> - Blood is all that matters - need to have maximum Vitea all the time. Get's Willpower when refilling Vitea in same scene.</li> <li><i>Monster</i> - Monster exists to torment, frighten, and destroy. She loathes existence, and spreads that loathing wherever she goes.</li> <li><i>Deviant</i> - Deviant lives to flout norms and break traditional expectations. She isn\u2019t concerned with rebellion; she\u2019s concerned with crime, sin, and debauchery.</li> <li><i>Puppeteer</i> - Blood is powerful bond. By chaining others to you, you regain you sense of control.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Got another idea to Beast Archetypes:<br /> <i>Terryfing</i> - Kindred lives to show how vampires are superior to others. Get's Willpower when showing other being that is better than them.<br /> <b>Comment:</b> Popular in Ordo Dracul, this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T03:02:01-08:00","id":1173722,"title":"","content":"Well duh VTR is bound to pay some homage to daddy, but if you really want you could use Vices and Virtues, not necessarily the Judeo-Christian version from 1ED but the fairly customizable one in Chronicles of Darkness corebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}